# Trained model artifacts — too large for git in general (the MovieLens-era
# latest.joblib exceeded GitHub's 100MB hard limit). The catalog-trained
# latest.joblib (see ml/train_from_catalog.py) is small (~1.2MB, real
# CoWatch catalog, not MovieLens) and is the only one the live router
# actually loads in prod, so it's the one exception — everything else in
# models/ (collaborative_latest.joblib, any other MovieLens artifact)
# stays ignored. meta.json/collaborative_meta.json are untouched by these
# rules — already tracked, and gitignore doesn't apply to tracked files.
models/*.joblib
!models/latest.joblib

# MLflow local tracking store — regenerated by training runs, ~1GB.
mlruns/
